{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Bruce Headlam is a Canadian journalist and the media desk editor of the "New York Times" since September 2008.","title":"Bruce Headlam"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He has reported in the several sections of the newspaper since 1998, including Circuits, Escapes and the Times Magazine.","title":"Bruce Headlam"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Previously he had worked at "Saturday Night Magazine" and "Canadian Business".","title":"Bruce Headlam"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He was featured in the film "".","title":"Bruce Headlam"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"NIGHT is an art/fashion/music/literature/nightlife periodical co-edited by Anton Perich and Robert Henry Rubin.","title":"NIGHT (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Established in Manhattan, New York, in 1978 the magazine was created during the punk-new wave-disco nightclub era of among others; Studio 54, Xenon, Club A, Regine's, The Continental, Hurrah's, Danceteria, and the Mudd Club.","title":"NIGHT (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Today the magazine continues to focus on the beautiful, the exclusive, the intelligent and the controversial.","title":"NIGHT (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Among the contributors have been; Charles Plymell, Helmut Newton.","title":"NIGHT (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Taylor Mead, Victor Bockris, Lee Klein, Charles Henri Ford and countless others.","title":"NIGHT (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" At the dawn of her writing career Sex in the City author Candace Bushnell wrote for NIGHT, stating... " “I wrote for this paper called Night Magazine, which was mainly just a bunch of pictures of people at Studio 54.","title":"NIGHT (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" I would do little interviews and profiles.”","title":"NIGHT (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":"...","title":"NIGHT (magazine)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Saturday Night Blues: 20 Years is a 2006 double CD compilation album, released by the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation and, internationally, by the Universal Music Group, of live performances of Canadian blues artists, as featured on the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation radio program, "Saturday Night Blues".","title":"Saturday Night Blues: 20 Years"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is a successor album to "Saturday Night Blues", released in 1991, which commemorated the radio program's fifth year.","title":"Saturday Night Blues: 20 Years"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ant & Dec's Saturday Night Takeaway, often referred to simply as Saturday Night Takeaway or SNT, is a British television variety show presented and executively produced by Ant & Dec.","title":"Ant &amp; Dec's Saturday Night Takeaway"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The show was first broadcast on 8 June 2002 on ITV.","title":"Ant &amp; Dec's Saturday Night Takeaway"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was broadcast live from The London Studios on the South Bank from 2002 till 2017.","title":"Ant &amp; Dec's Saturday Night Takeaway"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The format was heavily influenced by previous Saturday night light entertainment shows, most notably "Noel's House Party" and "Don't Forget Your Toothbrush", while individual items often pay homage to Saturday night TV of the past, such as "Opportunity Knocks".","title":"Ant &amp; Dec's Saturday Night Takeaway"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Saturday Night Magazine is a lifestyle and entertainment magazine created in 2004 at the University of Southern California by publisher and founder Michael Ritter.","title":"Saturday Night Magazine (U.S.)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" "Saturday Night Magazine" targets a readership of 18- to 29-year-olds through editorial coverage that includes: celebrities, fashion, sports, politics, music, technology, travel, careers, movies, video games, and comedy.","title":"Saturday Night Magazine (U.S.)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The median age of its readers is 23.","title":"Saturday Night Magazine (U.S.)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Past covers have featured celebrities and public figures such as: Katy Perry, Shenae Grimes, DJ AM, Emma Stone, Amber Heard, Sophia Bush, Rachel Bilson, Scarlett Johansson, Kristen Bell, Katie Couric, Audrina Patridge, Heidi Montag and Malin Åkerman.","title":"Saturday Night Magazine (U.S.)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It can be found on college campuses in Los Angeles, San Francisco, San Diego, Phoenix and Tucson, as well as at many off-campus retail locations.","title":"Saturday Night Magazine (U.S.)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In November 2008, "Saturday Night Magazine" celebrated its 40th issue.","title":"Saturday Night Magazine (U.S.)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The phrase Saturday night special is a colloquial term used in the United States and Canada for any inexpensive handgun, especially a mousegun/pocket pistol.","title":"Saturday night special"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Saturday night specials have been defined as compact, inexpensive, small-caliber handguns with perceived low quality; however, there is no official definition of "Saturday night special" under US or Canadian federal law.","title":"Saturday night special"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Some states define "Saturday night specials" or "junk guns" by means of composition or materials strength.","title":"Saturday night special"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Low cost and high availability make these weapons attractive to many buyers despite their shortcomings.","title":"Saturday night special"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In the late 19th century and early 20th century, they were commonly referred to as suicide specials.","title":"Saturday night special"}],"peer_messages":["Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Bruce Headlam is a Canadian journalist and the media desk editor of the \"New York Times\" since September 2008.","title":"Bruce Headlam"}
